                     <p>The Romsey attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                     Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement
                     (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card
                     records the following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an
                     attribution: <q>Provenance indicated by liturgical details.</q></p><p>
                     Additionally, this index card bears the following cross reference: <q>reject
                     [i.e. from Romsey] also Cotton Vit. A.vii</q>. For comparison, MLGB3
                     (2010-2015) recorded: Fols. 1–76 [of Additional MS 28188] are closely connected
                     wih Cotton Vit. A.vii fols. 17–112. </p></provenance>
